    {
      "id": "game-description-ae50f377-e500-4377-b418-272ed8a478a5-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Basketball is a court game in which teams score by sending a ball through an elevated hoop. Passing and dribbling move the ball into shooting positions, while screens, cuts, and rebounds create new opportunities. Standard full-court play uses five players per side, but playground and other small-team forms are also central to its culture."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-ae50f377-e500-4377-b418-272ed8a478a5-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "James Naismith devised the game in Springfield, Massachusetts, in December 1891 as an indoor activity for his students. Its original peach baskets and simple rules developed into a fast sport in which spacing, coordination, and individual ball skills constantly interact."
    },
